# React Native UI

## Platform
iOS and Android are production targets. Do not add web-only APIs or require web parity.

## Theming
Use `ThemedText`, `ThemedView`, and `useTheme()` — not raw `Text`/`View` with hardcoded colors.

Palette + spacing + radius: `@/constants/theme` (Serene Clinical — see `DESIGN.md`). Never define local `DESIGN` / hex color maps in screens.

```typescript
import { ThemedText } from '@/components/themed-text';
import { ThemedView } from '@/components/themed-view';
import { Spacing } from '@/constants/theme';

function MyScreen() {
  return (
    <ThemedView style={{ padding: Spacing.three }}>
      <ThemedText type="title">Record</ThemedText>
    </ThemedView>
  );
}
```

Use `Colors`, `Spacing`, `Fonts` from `@/constants/theme`. Use `StyleSheet.create` for component styles.

## Layer Separation
- `src/app/` — thin screens, route wiring only
- `src/components/` — reusable UI
- `src/hooks/` — screen logic, calls services
- `src/services/` — no React imports, no UI

## Platform Files
Use extension suffixes when needed: `Component.web.tsx`, `Component.ios.tsx`. Import normally — bundler resolves.

## Accessibility
Add `testID` to interactive elements. Use `accessibilityLabel` where `testID` is insufficient.

## English Only (V1)
User-facing strings in English. No i18n library until explicitly added.
